Create-project sections are tabbed, and member roles are per-person

Creating a project collects five sections; stacked one after another,
reaching "Files" meant scrolling past tasks and QA. They are tabs now —
Team, Tasks, QA, Files — the way the previous system grouped them. All
panels stay mounted and are only hidden; unmounting the inactive tab
would drop its inputs from FormData and the section would be silently
ignored.

The role dropdown beside a project member listed every role in the
system, so someone could be signed onto a project as a role they do not
hold — and the per-role effort report would then say something that was
never true. It now lists only the roles tagged on that person, and stays
empty until a person is chosen rather than inviting a choice that will
be rejected.

